<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <!--
    Spring Boot 3.3.x is the line that pairs with Java 21 and is what the
    eclipse-temurin:21 images run. The scaffold proposed a 4.x parent and
    three artifact ids that do not exist in Maven Central
    (spring-boot-starter-webmvc, -webmvc-test, -actuator-test). Those were
    replaced with the real ones: spring-boot-starter-web and
    spring-boot-starter-test.
  -->
  <parent>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>
    <version>3.3.5</version>
    <relativePath/>
  </parent>

  <groupId>com.example</groupId>
  <artifactId>app</artifactId>
  <version>0.0.1-SNAPSHOT</version>
  <name>gitops-monorepo-app</name>
  <description>Release-mode demo service for the GitOps monorepo platform</description>

  <properties>
    <java.version>21</java.version>
    <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>

    <!--
      ============================================================
      CVE PATCH LEVELS — these override the versions Boot 3.3.5 pins.
      ============================================================

      WHY: Boot 3.3.5 was released Nov 2024; its BOM freezes these trees at
      that date. The image scan (HIGH/CRITICAL, fixed-only, before push) found
      ~2 years of accumulated advisories:

        tomcat-embed-core   CVE-2024-50379 / -56337  RCE, TOCTOU in JSP compilation
                            CVE-2025-48988           DoS, multipart upload
                            CVE-2025-48989           DoS, HTTP/2 "MadeYouReset"
                            CVE-2025-52520 / -53506  DoS
                            CVE-2025-55752           directory traversal, possible RCE
                            CVE-2026-24734           certificate revocation bypass
        spring-expression   CVE-2026-41850           DoS via crafted SpEL
        spring-webmvc       CVE-2026-41842           DoS resolving static resources
                            CVE-2026-41845           XSS, incorrect JavaScript escaping

      THESE THREE MOVE TOGETHER — DO NOT BUMP ONE ALONE.
      Boot's BOM keeps Spring Framework and Micrometer in lockstep. A previous
      attempt raised spring-framework to 6.2.19 while leaving micrometer at the
      BOM's 1.13.6; requireUpperBoundDeps failed in the lint stage because
      spring-web 6.2.19 requires micrometer-observation 1.15.12. Overriding
      half of a coordinated version set is what causes that.

      EVERY VERSION HERE CAME FROM TOOL OUTPUT, NOT FROM MEMORY:
        - 10.1.52 and 6.2.19 — Trivy's "Fixed Version" column
        - 1.15.12            — the enforcer's own convergence report
      This repo has lost attempts to unverifiable external identifiers; taking
      the number from the tool that demanded it is the only safe source.

      MAINTENANCE: when the parent is next raised, DELETE all three properties
      and the dependencyManagement block below rather than carrying them
      forward — a stale downgrade-pin is worse than none. The enforcer in the
      lint stage will flag the conflict if they are left behind.
    -->
    <tomcat.version>10.1.52</tomcat.version>
    <spring-framework.version>6.2.19</spring-framework.version>
    <micrometer.version>1.15.12</micrometer.version>
  </properties>

  <!--
    BELT AND BRACES. The properties above are the supported override mechanism
    and should be sufficient on their own. This block pins the same artifacts
    explicitly so the build does not depend on the property NAME being right —
    if a property is spelled differently in this Boot line, the version here
    still wins, and if the properties work this block is simply redundant.
    Cheap insurance on a build that can only be exercised in CI.
  -->
  <dependencyManagement>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency>
        <groupId>io.micrometer</groupId>
        <artifactId>micrometer-bom</artifactId>
        <version>${micrometer.version}</version>
        <type>pom</type>
        <scope>import</scope>
      </dependency>
      <dependency>
        <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-framework-bom</artifactId>
        <version>${spring-framework.version}</version>
        <type>pom</type>
        <scope>import</scope>
      </dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </dependencyManagement>

  <dependencies>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
    </dependency>

    <!-- Health endpoint, remapped to /healthz in application.properties. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-actuator</artifactId>
    </dependency>

    <!--
      Without this, actuator's prometheus endpoint does not exist and the
      ServiceScrapes in gitops/scrapes/ would scrape a 404 forever.
      NOTE: the dependency alone is not sufficient — the endpoint must also be
      ENABLED in application.properties. Exposure is not enablement; that
      distinction cost two CI attempts.
    -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>io.micrometer</groupId>
      <artifactId>micrometer-registry-prometheus</artifactId>
    </dependency>

    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-test</artifactId>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <finalName>app</finalName>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
